{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "label": "TypedActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The runtime host that interprets a Behavior - an Actor subclass on the same mailbox, dispatcher and supervisor tree whose onReceive delegates to the currently active behavior. Never constructed directly, because the typed runtime needs a fresh instance on every restart."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_behavior_resolution_loop", "label": "Behavior resolution loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Composed behaviors unwrap one layer at a time - supervise, withTimers, setup - each running its side effect once and disappearing, until a receive leaf is stored as current. The strategy and timer scheduler are remembered for the actor's lifetime; the setup factory reruns only on restart."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_wrapper_cycle_bound", "label": "64-hop wrapper cycle bound", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A setup that returns itself, or a recursing supervise, would spin forever; the resolver throws after 64 hops so the misconfiguration surfaces loudly."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typed_lifecycle_signals", "label": "Typed lifecycle signals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "post-stop, pre-restart (carrying the error as signal.reason) and terminated (carrying the watched ref) are invoked from the framework's postStop, preRestart and Terminated delivery hooks; the return value transitions behavior exactly like a receive handler's."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_initial_behavior_edge_cases", "label": "Initial-behavior edge cases", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "same as the initial behavior is meaningless and is treated as empty, so the actor exists but drops everything - usually a logic bug. stopped as the initial behavior terminates in preStart, which is useful when an external check decides whether the actor should exist at all."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_behavior_resolution_loop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_behavior_resolution_loop", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_wrapper_cycle_bound", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_behavior_resolution_loop", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_setup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_behavior_resolution_loop", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors_supervise", "relation": "reference